    {
      "ordinal": 5,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "3.1",
      "title": "Bascinets with perforated and forehead attached visor",
      "body": "The term “Bascinets with perforated and forehead attached visor” will be abbreviated to “Perforated Klappvisor Bascinets” for the remainder of the document.\n\nPerforated Klappvisor Bascinets can be seen in a couple of manuscripts, from 1389 to 1420/1430.\n\nPerforated Klappvisor Bascinets can have a visor with a rounded profile or a sharp profile. The shape of the profile does not change the approved and denied time periods.\n\nPerforated Klappvisor Bascinets are Approved for Transitional armors.\n\nPerforated Klappvisor Bascinets are Denied for 14th century armors.\n\nPerforated Klappvisor Bascinets can be Approved for 15th century armors with a coherent project.\nWe strongly recommend sending an email to authenticity@buhurtinternational.com before placing an order for such armor.\n\nVindobonensis 2762, Wenzel Bible - 1389 - Austria Pal.lat.1888 - 1430 - Germany\n\nGöttinger MS Philos. 63 Bellifortis - 1405 - Germany",
      "page_from": 4,
      "page_to": 4,
      "stable_key": "perforated-visor-bascinets:3.1",
