    {
      "ordinal": 7,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "3.3",
      "title": "Great Bascinets with perforated visor",
      "body": "Later during the 15th-century, a handful of contemporary designs show the use of perforated visors, despite a great lack of representation in art.\n\nGreat Bascinets with perforated visors must have a visor with a rounded profile.\n\nGreat Bascinets with perforated visors are Approved for 15th century armors.\n\nGreat Bascinets with perforated visors are Denied for 14th century and Transitional armors.\n\nGerman Great Bascinet, MET\n\nGrand Bacinet private collection - 1450/1475- southern Germany or Austria",
